WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.361
Bhopal, 2 December 1984.

2
00:00:06.501 --> 00:00:09.148
A city sleeps beside a pesticide plant.

3
00:00:09.508 --> 00:00:13.107
The Union Carbide plant made pesticides for
Indian farms.

4
00:00:13.247 --> 00:00:17.299
Its tanks held methyl isocyanate, a chemical
that attacks the lungs.

5
00:00:17.439 --> 00:00:20.388
Tank 610 held about forty-two tonnes of it.

6
00:00:20.528 --> 00:00:22.757
The safety systems were not all working.

7
00:00:23.117 --> 00:00:26.600
The official inquiry found water had entered
Tank 610.

8
00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:28.296
Pressure and temperature climbed.

9
00:00:28.436 --> 00:00:30.770
The refrigeration unit had been shut down.

10
00:00:30.910 --> 00:00:34.219
The flare tower was offline, and the scrubber
could not cope.

11
00:00:34.359 --> 00:00:36.368
No public warning prepared the city.

12
00:00:36.728 --> 00:00:38.678
Around midnight, the tank vented.

13
00:00:38.818 --> 00:00:42.359
A cloud of MIC rolled low over the railway
colony and the old city.

14
00:00:42.499 --> 00:00:44.867
People woke with burning eyes and no breath.

15
00:00:45.007 --> 00:00:48.177
They ran into the dark, away from a smell they
could not name.

16
00:00:48.317 --> 00:00:51.103
The gas moved through the streets before the
city understood.

17
00:00:51.463 --> 00:00:55.225
The official immediate death toll was 2,259.

18
00:00:55.365 --> 00:00:59.417
Madhya Pradesh later confirmed 3,787 deaths.

19
00:00:59.557 --> 00:01:04.851
Survivors' clinics estimate 8,000 died in the
first weeks, and 8,000 more since.

20
00:01:04.991 --> 00:01:07.812
More than 500,000 people were exposed.

21
00:01:08.172 --> 00:01:13.396
In 1989, the Supreme Court approved a $470
million settlement.

22
00:01:13.536 --> 00:01:16.253
The claims were consolidated under the Indian
government.

23
00:01:16.393 --> 00:01:20.422
Union Carbide's chairman was charged in India,
but never extradited.

24
00:01:20.562 --> 00:01:23.523
In 2010, seven former employees were
convicted.

25
00:01:23.583 --> 00:01:25.740
The sentence was two years.

26
00:01:25.880 --> 00:01:28.074
The settlement did not end the argument.

27
00:01:28.434 --> 00:01:31.429
The plant stopped production in 1986.

28
00:01:31.569 --> 00:01:34.007
Its waste and contaminated water remained.

29
00:01:34.147 --> 00:01:36.933
Survivors still carry the exposure in their
bodies.

30
00:01:37.073 --> 00:01:39.708
Groundwater near the site is still
contaminated.

31
00:01:40.068 --> 00:01:41.960
Every year, Bhopal remembers.

32
00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:46.814
The disaster helped push India's Environment
Protection Act in 1986.

33
00:01:46.954 --> 00:01:49.694
It did not settle the question of who was
responsible.

34
00:01:49.834 --> 00:01:53.503
The memorial is a wall, a flame, and an
unfinished argument.

35
00:01:53.863 --> 00:01:55.407
The gas lasted one night.

36
00:01:55.547 --> 00:01:57.672
The claims have lasted four decades.
